    ],
    "summary": "A virgin from Nazareth, engaged to Joseph of Nazareth. Luke describes Gabriel announcing that she will bear Jesus, and her reply, “Behold the handmaid of the Lord”. She visits her relative Elisabeth and sings a prayer praising God. Luke places Jesus' birth in Bethlehem, where Mary lays him in a feeding trough. She presents him in the temple and later finds him there among the teachers. John places her at Cana's wedding and the cross, where Jesus entrusts her to the disciple he loved. Acts names her among those gathered after Jesus' ascent.",
