    "aliases": [
      "John the baptist",
      "Baptist John"
    ],
    "summary": "Zacharias and Elisabeth's son. Luke places the announcement to Mary in Elisabeth's sixth month of pregnancy, without giving an exact interval between births. Matthew describes John preaching changed lives in Judaea's wilderness, wearing camel hair and eating locusts and wild honey. He baptizes people who confess their sins in the Jordan. Luke records advice to crowds, soldiers and tax collectors; Matthew describes his rebuke of Pharisees and Sadducees. He baptizes Jesus, and John records his statement that Jesus must increase while he decreases. After rebuking Herod over Herodias, he is imprisoned. He sends disciples to question Jesus before the account of his execution.",
