      "Herod"
    ],
    "summary": "King of Judaea when Matthew places Jesus' birth. “Great” is a conventional label, not his quoted KJV name. Visiting wise men ask about the newborn king, troubling Herod and Jerusalem. Religious leaders name Bethlehem, and he tells the visitors to report back. Matthew says their return by another road angers him. He orders the killing of children aged two and under in Bethlehem and nearby areas. After his death, Matthew describes Joseph bringing the family from Egypt. Luke places John's birth in his reign. He is distinct from Herod the tetrarch and the Herod in Acts known as Agrippa.",
