    ],
    "summary": "A fisherman from Bethsaida, Andrew's brother, called Simon and named Peter by Jesus. Luke describes him leaving his nets after an extraordinary catch. The Gospels' calling accounts are kept distinct here. Peter comes first in lists of the Twelve. Matthew describes him walking on water, sinking and declaring, “Thou art the Christ, the Son of the living God”. Jesus rebukes him for resisting the warning of his coming suffering and death. Peter sees Jesus transformed on the mountain and later promises not to deny him. After the arrest, he denies Jesus three times and weeps. John describes his tomb visit and the risen Jesus asking about his love and directing him to feed his sheep.",
