    "summary": "A Pharisee, a member of a Jewish religious group, and a leader who visits Jesus at night in John. He says Jesus' miracles show God is with him. Jesus speaks of being born again through water and the Spirit: a new birth Nicodemus struggles to understand. The dialogue turns to the raised serpent and God's love in John 3:16. In John 7, Nicodemus asks whether the law judges someone before hearing him. After the crucifixion, he brings about a hundred pounds of myrrh and aloes, substances used in preparing a body. He helps Joseph of Arimathaea bury Jesus.",
