    "summary": "The Roman governor of Judaea before whom Jesus appears after his arrest. The Gospels record him asking, “Art thou the King of the Jews?” and declaring no fault. Luke describes him sending Jesus to Herod. The accounts also describe the offer involving Barabbas; Matthew adds his wife's warning and his hand washing. He has Jesus whipped and hands him over for crucifixion. John gives the cross inscription as “Jesus Of Nazareth The King Of The Jews”. He grants Joseph of Arimathaea the body. Matthew describes a guard at the tomb. Luke 13:1 mentions Galileans whose blood Pilate mixed with their sacrifices.",
